			<key>WFWorkflowActionIdentifier</key>
			<string>is.workflow.actions.comment</string>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionParameters</key>
			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>CC Launch — Home Screen launcher for starting Claude Code sessions on the Mac. Type or speak a free-text entry (with optional flags), or fall back to a grouped list.

How it works: first you get a text box where you can type or dictate an entry such as 'ebay' or 'ebay sonnet high' (the keyboard's mic key dictates; typing lets you add flags). That answer is saved as typed. If typed has any value, it becomes the phrase verbatim and the list is skipped. If you leave it blank, a single flat list (Launch what?) appears with Projects, Skills, and Folders grouped under non-tappable section header rows; picking a real row saves a short phrase. After that, if phrase is empty (blank box plus a header tapped, or nothing chosen) you get a 'nothing selected' notification and nothing is sent. Otherwise a single Get Contents of URL posts the phrase to the Mac trigger and a notification shows what was sent plus the server reply.

Primary endpoint (wired): http://n8server.tail962d9.ts.net:8923/trigger (POST).
LAN fallback (NOT wired): http://192.168.4.112:8923/trigger — when off Tailscale, swap the URL in the Get Contents of URL action.

Auth and body: the request sends a JSON body like {"phrase":"ebay"}, and the Bearer secret is already embedded in the single Get Contents of URL action's Authorization header, so there is zero setup — just import and run.

Import note: if a shortcut named CC Launch already exists in your library, delete it first or this import will be silently skipped.</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionIdentifier</key>
			<string>is.workflow.actions.comment</string>
			<key>WFWorkflowActionParameters</key>
			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>Shortcuts generated by Shortcuts Playground. May contain mistakes. Always check the shortcut's actions first.

This shortcut was created via the following user prompt:

&gt; Modify "CC Launch" so the front-end lets the user type OR speak a free-text entry (with optional flags) BEFORE the menu. Add a first Ask for Input (Text) saved to a variable typed; if typed has any value use it as the phrase, otherwise show the same flat grouped Choose from Menu (minus the old "type or speak" row) to set the phrase. Keep the HTTP request exactly: one Get Contents of URL, POST to the Mac trigger with a hardcoded Bearer token and a JSON body with one phrase field, then a result notification. Guard: if phrase has any value POST and notify, otherwise show a 'nothing selected' notification.</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
